what = IntroWhat(
  "A powerful effects subsystem in PixiJS that enables blurs, color grading, displacement maps, glows, outlines, and custom GLSL/WGSL shaders with automatic bounding box padding and render target pooling.",
  "PixiJS Filters are post-processing shader programs that intercept the rendering of a DisplayObject or Container, capture its output into an offscreen RenderTarget, and execute GPU fragment shaders to transform pixels.",
  [
    "Post-Processing Pipeline: Intercepts display tree rendering into offscreen framebuffers",
    "Built-in & Community Filters: Blur, ColorMatrix, Displacement, Noise, Glow, Outline, Shockwave",
    "Custom GLSL Shaders: Write custom vertex and fragment shaders with animated uniforms",
    "FilterSystem & Resource Pooling: Reusable RenderTarget pools to prevent VRAM memory churn",
  ],
  ["PixiJS", "GLSL", "WebGL", "Shaders", "Post-Processing"],
)

why = IntroWhy(
  "Standard 2D sprite rendering is limited to linear tinting and alpha blending. Creating atmospheric effects like heat distortion, bloom, chromatic aberration, or dynamic drop shadows requires per-pixel fragment manipulation.",
  "PixiJS Filters provide hardware-accelerated post-processing without writing complex framebuffer ping-pong pipelines from scratch, giving 2D games and web applications studio-grade visual polish.",
)
